    <section aria-labelledby="limits">
      <h2 id="limits">11. Limits and open questions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Viikki measures NEE in about 20 % of the periods. It has few valid <Fragment set:html={f.e0} /> windows, and the <Fragment set:html={f.rrefSym} /> interpolation spans long winter gaps.
        </li>
        <li>
          Maktau: only 2019 is almost complete. 2018 and 2023 use <Fragment set:html={f.e0} /> of a neighbour year. 2023 has
          no Reco, because the few measured night fluxes are negative.
        </li>
        <li>
          Anttila, Särkisuo, Haltiala and Viikki have no <Fragment set:html={f.ustar} /> in the files. We use the quality
          flag of the provider.
        </li>
        <li>Särkisuo 2023 has an 84-day gap in the air temperature. Thus it has no annual GPP and Reco.</li>
        <li>
          The NECB is a lower bound in years with an organic input of unknown carbon content. One compost application can
          hold about 500 g C m<sup>−2</sup>, more than the annual NEE.
        </li>
        <li>
          The Viikki yields have no unit. The Haltiala 2025 yield can be a fresh mass. Two Qvidja dry-matter fractions are
          not certain.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="reproduce">
